; Push the command's words that follow the noun
;
; Same as #R$7E7C but with the opposite test: a word of the command record is
; pushed when its "before the noun" flag is clear. Sets the two JR opcodes of
; #R$7E7C to JR Z ($28) and continues there.
;
; O:stack Two words for the message printer's {WORD} codes, see #R$7E7C
@label=PushWordsAfter
c$7E78 LD A,$28           ; $28 = JR Z
 $7E7A JR $7E7E      ;
